  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A solid cylindrical wheel, initially at rest, rolls down a slope without slipping from a vertical height of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0\\: \\textup{m}\"></span>. The moment of inertia, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span>, for the wheel is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{1}{2}mr^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is the radius of the wheel.</p>\n<p>What is the best estimate for the final linear speed of the wheel?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{30} \\; \\textup{m s}^{-1}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{40} \\; \\textup{m s}^{-1}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{60} \\; \\textup{m s}^{-1}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{80} \\; \\textup{m s}^{-1}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
